        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.844,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "3. For each statement identify the appropriate algebraic expression(s)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.112,
            0.823,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "(i) Two more than a square number. $2 + s$ $( s + 2 ) ^ { 2 }$ $s ^ { 2 } + 2$ $s ^ { 2 } + 4$ $2 s ^ { 2 }$ $2 ^ { 2 } s$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.156,
            0.799,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The sum of the squares of two consecutive numbers $m ^ { 2 } + n ^ { 2 }$ $( m + n ) ^ { 2 }$ $m ^ { 2 } + 1$ $m ^ { 2 } + ( m + 1 ) ^ { 2 }$ $m^{2}+(m-1)^{2}\\quad(m+(m+1))^{2}\\quad(2m)^{2}+(2m+1)^{2}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.223,
            0.205,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.253,
            0.662,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "(i) Two more than a square numbers is $s ^ { 2 } + 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.278,
            0.776,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The sum of the squares of two consecutive numbers is $m ^ { 2 } + ( m + 1 ) ^ { 2 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.328,
            0.847,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": "4. the figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.371,
            0.648,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"7\">February</td></tr><tr><td>Su</td><td>M</td><td>Tu</td><td>W</td><td>Th</td><td>F</td><td>Sa</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>5</td><td>6</td><td>7</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>10</td><td>11</td><td>12</td><td>13</td><td>14</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>17</td><td>18</td><td>19</td><td>20</td><td>21</td><td>22</td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>24</td><td>25</td><td>26</td><td>27</td><td>28</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_30_table_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.546,
            0.847,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "Find products of numbers lying along each diagonal — $4 \\times 1 2 = 4 8 ,$ 5 × 11 = 55. Do this for the other 2 by 2 squares. What do you observe about the diagonal products? Explain why this happens. **Hint:** Label the numbers in each 2 by 2 square as"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.689,
            0.26,
            0.707
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans. Take,"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.67,
            0.368,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "| 3 | 4 |\n| --- | --- |\n| 10 | 11 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_30_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.742,
            0.38,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "Her $\\mathrm{e}, \\quad 3 \\times 11 = 33$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.762,
            0.379,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": "4 \\times 10 = 40",
          "image_source": "images/page_30_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.782,
            0.71,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "We observe that difference of diagonal products = 7 **Reason:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.821,
            0.613,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": "| a | (a + 1) |\n| --- | --- |\n| a + 7 | (a + 8) |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_30_table_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.879,
            0.741,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "We have diagonal difference = (a + 7) (a + 1) – (a + 8) = 7"
        },
        {
